{"questions":[{"question_id":"oU6nrcM46dLaoyPq","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"physics","chapter":"units-and-measurements","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"vernier-calipers","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"the-diameter-of-a-cylinder-is-measured-using-a-vernier-calli-2013-marks-4-ou6nrcm46dlaoypq.htm","content":"The diameter of a cylinder is measured using a Vernier callipers with no zero error. It is found that the zero\nof the Vernier scale lies between 5.10 cm and 5.15 cm of the main scale. The Vernier scale has 50 divisions\nequivalent to 2.45 cm. The 24<sup>th</sup> division of the Vernier scale exactly coincides with one of the main scale\ndivisions. The diameter of the cylinder is","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"5.112 cm"},{"identifier":"B","content":"5.124 cm"},{"identifier":"C","content":"5.136 cm"},{"identifier":"D","content":"5.148 cm"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>From the given data :</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>One main scale division (MSD) is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"30.068ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 13290 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(1778,0)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scal